# MIS standard CODEOWNERS
#
# Place at .github/CODEOWNERS in the repo root. GitHub auto-requests
# review from the listed owners on any PR that touches matching paths,
# and at least one owner approval is required to merge.
#
# Format: <path-pattern>  <@user-or-team>...
# Later rules override earlier ones. Use @org/team-name for team handles.

# Fallback: every file has an owner so nothing slips through.
*                           @MIS-org/eng-leads

# Backend / API
/api/                       @MIS-org/backend
/services/                  @MIS-org/backend
/migrations/                @MIS-org/backend @MIS-org/dba

# Frontend / web / mobile
/web/                       @MIS-org/frontend
/app/                       @MIS-org/frontend
/mobile/                    @MIS-org/frontend

# Infrastructure / DevOps
/infra/                     @MIS-org/devops
/.github/                   @MIS-org/devops
/.github/workflows/         @MIS-org/devops
/Dockerfile                 @MIS-org/devops
/docker-compose*.yml        @MIS-org/devops

# Security-sensitive files — require security review
/auth/                      @MIS-org/security @MIS-org/backend
**/secrets*                 @MIS-org/security

# Docs — anyone in eng can approve
*.md                        @MIS-org/eng
/docs/                      @MIS-org/eng
